  era: "1st c. CE \xB7 Section 8 \xB7 Post-Mauryan India \xB7 c. 200 BCE \u2013 300 CE"
  title: Trade with Rome
  text: Trade boomed. Indian pepper, spices, textiles, gems and ivory went to the Roman empire, and Roman gold coins and wine came back. Ports such as Barygaza, now Bharuch, and Muziris thrived, and merchant guilds funded monasteries and caves.
